\section{Extended SNR Analysis}
\label{app:snr_extended}

To verify that KL's gradient signal advantage persists beyond the initial training phase (\S\ref{sec:method:gradient}), we measure per-layer gradient SNR at 7 checkpoints (steps 0, 50, 100, 150, 200, 250, 300) with 95\% bootstrap confidence intervals.
The KL/BCE SNR ratio remains stable throughout training: from the initial gap at step 0, KL maintains $5.14\times$ higher average SNR at step 300 ($5.88{\times}10^{-3}$ vs.\ $1.14{\times}10^{-3}$). % exp_id: snr_extended_r6w3
The ratio is consistent across layers and does not converge as BCE training progresses, confirming that the SNR advantage reflects a structural property of end-to-end coupling rather than a transient artifact of early optimization.


